# The intersection of two intervals of the round-up interval (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Hull
# and intersection"): the smaller lane of each, min(b, d) and min(-a, -c) = -max(a, c); the empty set
# when an operand is empty or when the lanes cross, u < -n, tested on the negated lane, exactly.
# Exact, in every rounding mode. Requires the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the
# options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_intersection_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
input:         pair stored y = yu yn
output:        pair z = zu zn
requires:      upward xu xn
requires:      upward yu yn
ensures:       interval_set zu zn intersection x=xu,xn y=yu,yn
min_precision: 1
source:        the smaller lanes, the empty set if they cross (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeUpwardExact.v upward_intersection_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the lanes are selected among the lanes of the operands and the NaN of the empty set; interval_set states what comes out for every pair of canonical states

mu = lt(yu, xu)                | mn = lt(yn, xn)
lu = select(mu, yu, xu)        | ln = select(mn, yn, xn)          # the smaller lanes
nu = neg(lu)                   | nn = neg(ln)
cu = lt(lu, nn)                | cn = lt(ln, nu)                  # u < -n: crossed (one mask, both lanes)
eu = unord(xu, yu)             | en = unord(xn, yn)               # an operand is empty
bu = or(eu, cu)                | bn = or(en, cn)
zu = select(bu, const nan, lu) | zn = select(bn, const nan, ln)
